    "What is your relationship with mathematics?": "I’ve always had a complicated relationship with math. It’s not my favorite subject, but I recognize its importance, especially in fields like economics and philosophy, which I dislike. My parents didn’t have much formal education, so I never got strong support at home. Still, I try to push through because it’s necessary for my part-time job in data analysis.",
    "Do you ever get anxious when thinking about mathematics?": "Absolutely. Math makes me nervous, especially when dealing with complex equations or statistics. My low conscientiousness means I often procrastinate on math tasks until the last minute, which only adds to the anxiety. Even simple problems can feel overwhelming sometimes.",
    "Did you ever use AI to support your math learning in the last year? If yes, how was your experience?": "Yes, I tried using an AI tutor for algebra last semester. It helped break down steps clearly, but my high neuroticism made me doubt its answers. Still, it reduced some anxiety by giving instant feedback.",
    "How would you explain, step by step, how to solve a second order algebraic equation?": "First, write the equation in standard form: ax² + bx + c = 0. Then, calculate the discriminant (b² - 4ac). If positive, there are two real roots; if zero, one root; if negative, no real roots. Use the quadratic formula: x = [-b ± √(discriminant)] / (2a) to find solutions.",
    "How would you explain, step by step, how to find the stationary points of an equation y=f(x)?": "Stationary points occur where the derivative f'(x) = 0. First, find the first derivative of f(x). Set it equal to zero and solve for x. These x-values are critical points. To confirm if they’re maxima or minima, check the second derivative: positive means minimum, negative means maximum.",
    "Briefly, how do you perform a Principal Component Analysis? Should I get anxious about its mathematics? Please, teach me.": "PCA simplifies data by reducing dimensions. You standardize variables, compute covariance matrix, find eigenvalues/eigenvectors, and project data onto top eigenvectors. The math is complex, but tools like Python’s scikit-learn handle it automatically. Don’t stress—focus on interpreting results.",
    "According to you, how can LLMs be used to innovate math learning in schools and universities?": "LLMs could personalize math education by adapting explanations to a student’s level. They could generate practice problems, provide instant feedback, and even simulate real-world applications, like using history or art (my favorite subjects) to make abstract concepts relatable."
